#   (run 2: the same with -t "^(?!.*turns Grok starts itself)", the six existing cases only, as a control for the afterAll)
# commits: run 0 (final, --reporter=verbose) at 39686a67ac; runs 1-2 at eb7dcef228 + the same test changes uncommitted.
# node v22.23.1; macOS 26.5.2; 2026-11-20
# machine: load average 42-84 from other processes, fseventsd ~195% CPU (an FSEvents backlog); no load imposed.
#
# Case -> AC:
#   "shows Grok's own turn after a background job ended ..."       AC-001 (TURN_STARTED, SYSTEM_TASK_NOTIFICATION
#       sender system.grok_provider_turn with the reminder text unwrapped, reasoning/text, tool card, usage,
#       TURN_COMPLETED; run reads running from the turn's start to its end, idle after) and AC-003 (the notice in
#       getRunProjection's conversation, what a reload reads)
#   "holds a message sent during Grok's own turn ... Stop cancels ..." AC-002 (the held message's turn starts after the
#       provider TURN_COMPLETED, answered, no ERROR / refused SEND_MESSAGE, 2 session/prompt in total; INTERRUPT_GENERATION
#       -> session/cancel -> TURN_INTERRUPTED)
#   "keeps a message held through the hand-over ..."               AC-006 (order probe 2 A: input end, provider
#       TURN_STARTED + notice, the held message's turn only after the provider TURN_COMPLETED, never failed, exactly
#       2 session/prompt: none sent while one was outstanding)
#
# First attempt (before the fix): AC-001's case failed at its status check: AGENT_STATUS running is published just
# before TURN_STARTED (for input turns as well), and the assertion looked for it after; the frame dump showed
#   AGENT_STATUS idle | AGENT_STATUS running | TURN_STARTED <provider> | SYSTEM_TASK_NOTIFICATION | ... | TURN_COMPLETED | AGENT_STATUS idle
# The assertion now reads the status in force at TURN_STARTED and at the end. Product behaviour unchanged.
#
# afterAll "Hook timed out in 60000ms" in both runs: the in-process server's app.close() under the FSEvents backlog
# (known: tickets/done/followups-483-517 IMP-04 timed it at 296,921 ms). Run 2 shows it without the new cases.

